#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:66
msgid ""
"When CSan detects a race, it writes a report to standard error. A watchpoint "
"report normally identifies both conflicting accesses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:77
msgid ""
"A value change without a matching instrumented access is reported as a `data "
"race of unknown origin` and contains only the sampled access. GPU reports "
"also identify the block, thread, and lane and may name the global variable "
"containing the raced address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:82
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:84
msgid ""
"The instrumentation marks memory accesses with a runtime function. The "
"runtime then samples these accesses. Sampling is fundamentally stalling a "
"given value while checking if any other threads have touched it during that "
"window. This is done using a **watchpoint** table and by **value "
"comparison**. Each probed access sets up a tripwire and checks later if "
"another thread triggered it like in the following pseudocode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:119
msgid ""
"The probability of detecting a race and the overhead of the sanitizer is "
"directly related to the probability of sampling and the length of the delay. "
"The watchpoint table can be omitted to make a minimal detector with less "
"coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:123
msgid "`__SANITIZE_CONCURRENCY__`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:125
msgid "Code can test whether CSan instrumentation is enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:133
msgid "Disabling instrumentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:135
msgid ""
"Use `no_sanitize(\"concurrency\")` to disable CSan memory-access "
"instrumentation for a function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:145
msgid ""
"The `disable_sanitizer_instrumentation` attribute disables all sanitizer "
"instrumentation and takes precedence over `no_sanitize` attributes. Use "
"either form carefully: uninstrumented accesses cannot consume watchpoints "
"and may reduce detection or produce reports of unknown origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:150
msgid "Run-time flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:152
msgid "CSan reads options from the `CSAN_OPTIONS` environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:158
msgid "The CSan-specific host options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:160
msgid ""
"`skip_watch` (default: `4000`): Approximate number of accesses skipped by a "
"thread before arming another watchpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:162
msgid ""
"`udelay` (default: `80`): Microseconds to delay after arming a watchpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:163
msgid ""
"`halt_on_error` (default: `false`): Terminate after the first host report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:165
msgid ""
"These options currently control the host detector. The AMDGPU sampling rate "
"and delay interval are fixed. Common sanitizer options still control "
"facilities such as symbolization and report formatting on the host side of "
"GPU reporting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:169
msgid ""
"Use `CSAN_OPTIONS=help=1` to print all CSan and sanitizer-common options. "
"Programs may provide host defaults by defining:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:178
msgid "Environment options take precedence over `__csan_default_options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:180
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:182
msgid ""
"CSan is probabilistic. It detects races that overlap a sampled observation "
"window rather than proving that a program is race-free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:184
msgid ""
"CSan does not implement ThreadSanitizer's happens-before model, lock-order "
"analysis, thread history, or synchronization diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:186
msgid ""
"CSan cannot be combined with several other full sanitizers, including "
"ThreadSanitizer and AddressSanitizer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:189
msgid "Security considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:191
msgid ""
"ConcurrencySanitizer is a testing tool. Its runtime is not intended for "
"production executables and was not developed under security-sensitive "
"runtime constraints. Instrumented programs deliberately change scheduling "
"and reserve additional memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:196
msgid "Current status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:198
msgid ""
"ConcurrencySanitizer is experimental. Its interface, reports, supported "
"targets, sampling policy, and run-time options may change. The compiler-rt "
"test suite can be run with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConcurrencySanitizer.md:206
msgid ""
"Minimized test cases and reports from real CPU and GPU applications are "
"welcome."
msgstr ""
